### Valuation Methodology

**rNPV formula:** `rNPV = (Peak Sales × Royalty Rate × PoS_combined) / (1 + discount_rate)^years_to_royalty`

**Inputs:**
- **NSCLC BrM market:** ~50,000 new NSCLC BrM cases/year in the US (SEER data). ~30% are ZEB1-high (Nagaishi 2017: 59% of BrM specimens, conservative adjustment for clinical threshold). ~7.5% are PTEN-null (cBioPortal bm_nsclc_mskcc_2023, n=322). ~24% are SPP1-high (DepMap-derived estimate).
- **Peak sales comparables:** Osimertinib (NSCLC BrM approved): $5.7B peak sales (AstraZeneca 2024 annual report). Pembrolizumab (NSCLC): $25B peak sales (Merck 2024). Cilengitide (off-patent, no current sales): $0 — value is in the indication + biomarker, not the compound.
- **Royalty rate:** 3–6% for method-of-treatment + companion diagnostic licensing (comparable precision oncology transactions: Repare/Roche, Foundation Medicine/Roche, HalioDx/Merck).
- **Discount rate:** 12% (standard pharma licensing discount rate).
- **PoS by evidence tier:**

| Evidence Tier | Phase II PoS | Phase III PoS | Approval PoS | Combined PoS |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| CRISPR-validated SL (Brief #1, #4) | 45% | 55% | 85% | **21%** |
| Mechanistically grounded (Brief #3) | 30% | 45% | 80% | **11%** |
| Computational hypothesis (Brief #2) | 20% | 40% | 80% | **6%** |

> PoS inputs: Wong et al. 2018 (Nature Biotechnology) — overall oncology Phase II→III 31%, Phase III→approval 58%. Biomarker-selected trials: +10–15% uplift vs. unselected (Jardim et al. 2021, Cancer Cell). CRISPR-validated SL: additional uplift based on Repare camonsertib Phase I→II transition data.

